---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Baby Safety Site"
  description="What this site does, where its recall data comes from, and how often it updates."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl p-4">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">About this site</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-base-content/80">
      A small, fast page for checking whether baby and child products have been recalled.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">What it does</h2>
      <p>
        The home page lists recent recalls of children's products, newest first. Each card links to
        the official recall notice, and expands to show consumer contact details and the retailers
        that sold the item.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        Every recall shown here comes from the <a
          href="https://www.saferproducts.gov/RestWebServices/Recall"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary">U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission</a
        > public recalls API, filtered to the children's product category.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing is written or edited by hand — this site only reformats what the CPSC publishes. It
        is not affiliated with or endorsed by the CPSC. For anything official, follow the link on a
        recall card through to <span class="font-medium">cpsc.gov</span>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">How current it is</h2>
      <p>
        Recalls are fetched when the site is built and published, so the list reflects the most
        recent deploy. The <span class="font-medium">↻ Refresh</span> button on the home page pulls live
        results straight from the CPSC if you want to be certain you are seeing the newest data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="alert alert-warning">
      <span>
        This site is an informational convenience, not a safety guarantee. An item not appearing
        here does not mean it has not been recalled.
      </span>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
